her config value for functional test.  Currently, if a developer sets inline_host_acquisition=False in their local shadow_config, this functional test fails. Make the test more hermetic by mocking out this value.  BUG=None TEST=Functional test finally passes with my modified shadow_config.  Change-Id: Id57bd345ea5cb9e1d0c78c39b75f90102354b4aa Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/422655 Commit-Ready: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="422655" owner_email="pprabhu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/55/422655/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I68511af87351c731cd6596856fbb9ffb7185af2d" commit="acebcd1b1db0285648b4f35ebf9f1ff2b5d84daf" commit_message="ANDROID: DEBUG: cpufreq: fix cpu_capacity tracing build for non-smp systems  cpu curr capacity can only be traced for SMP systems. Non-SMP builds will fail with:  drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq.c: In function cpufreq_freq_transition_begin: drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq.c:438:22: error: implicit declaration of function capacity_curr_of [-Werror=implicit-function-declaration]    trace_cpu_capacity(capacity_curr_of(cpu), cpu);                       ^ BUG=chromium:676723 TEST=Build with CPU_FREQ enabled and SMP disabled  Fixes: Change-Id: Icd0930d11068fcb7d2b6a9a48e7ed974904e1081        (&quot;DEBUG: sched,cpufreq: add cpu_capacity change tracepoint&quot;) Signed-off-by: Amit Pundir &lt;amit.pundir@linaro.org&gt; [jstultz: Cherry-picked from common/android-3.18] Signed-off-by: John Stultz &lt;john.stultz@linaro.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 6c7e03dde14e5074134f47d9ec3dea7de24e4e58) Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I68511af87351c731cd6596856fbb9ffb7185af2d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423332 Commit-Ready: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423332" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/32/423332/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I6808e82a8f213a247752b784abce6400b4e87f6b" commit="eb66152b3511f3a5f3efd88ec15dcf20341b79e9" commit_message="ANDROID: arm: Fix build error &quot;conflicting types for 'scale_cpu_capacity'&quot;  Commit &quot;arm: Update arch_scale_cpu_capacity() to reflect change to define&quot; introduced a dependency on struct sched_domain in arch/arm/include/asm/topologoy.h, but that structure is only currently defined if CONFIG_CPU_FREQ is enabled, which causes include/linux/cpufreq.h to get pulled in which defines it.  Include &lt;linux/cpufreq.h&gt; regardless of CONFIG_CPU_FREQ so struct sched_domain is always defined.  Fixes: Change-Id: I372bd5e4c1e203428d72b18c8a806b06f3567ef6        (&quot;arm: Update arch_scale_cpu_capacity() to reflect change to define&quot;) Signed-off-by: Steve Muckle &lt;smuckle@linaro.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Amit Pundir &lt;amit.pundir@linaro.org&gt; [jstultz: Cherry-picked from android-3.18] Signed-off-by: John Stultz &lt;john.stultz@linaro.org&gt;  BUG=chromium:676729 TEST=Build image with CONFIG_CPU_FREQ disabled  (cherry picked from commit ad607cd620b8caeebf3ed3336fa80921c588b27f) Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I6808e82a8f213a247752b784abce6400b4e87f6b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423436 Commit-Ready: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423436" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/36/423436/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ic4ee7fb4af43739aff441ce6dd155d57d8a1eaf8" commit="2bef4a51ecdb7778fb20f6e60f8116515819466b" commit_message="HACK: ARM: dts: rockchip: Make DDRFreq even more prone to stay high freq  It looks very likely that DDRFreq is responsible for some of the cursor jank I've been seeing.  Let's bump up the levels just a little more to make it even more likely that we'll stay at higher rates (but it's still possible we'll end up at the lower rates).  This is a bit of a workaround till we figure out how to deal with the jank better.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:61284 TEST=Seems less janky; still see 400 MHz, 666 MHz, 928 MHz being used.  Change-Id: Ic4ee7fb4af43739aff441ce6dd155d57d8a1eaf8 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423392 Reviewed-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423392" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/92/423392/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idebe1931bdbede9d03680c127f75e5a2fc1e8883" commit="3125d2321b8a899478daf4ae30d0d62bdcf3ccd9" commit_message="kevin/gru: modify platform-cpuset for usage of schedtune cgroups  This uses the schedtune boosting to make sure we hit 60fps compositing while still allowing these threads to run on little cores if the bigs get overloaded.  This results in a nice improvement to page load times.  We also need to use the sched governor to use schedtune.  BUG=chromes-os-partner:58667 TEST=build/boot on kevin CQ-DEPEND=CL:422419  Change-Id: Idebe1931bdbede9d03680c127f75e5a2fc1e8883 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423228 Commit-Ready: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423228" owner_email="sonnyrao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/28/423228/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I72a3ffd99a3dadf06c6bb042a5a19b02645ecd5d" commit="f37f5da2ba7f0fa0eeb3cd5377c4571df0f5c3c4" commit_message="Waiting for USB ethernet dongle without stopping the shill.  The upstart script moblab-network-bridge-init.conf will block 5 minutes to wait for the USB ethnet dongle ready. We used to stop the shill during the wait. This cause the Moblab to have no external interet connection during the time. Also if the dongle is not configured, shill is not restarted. We fix this by only stop the shill when USB dongle is detected.  BUG=chromium:630034 TEST=manual.  Change-Id: I72a3ffd99a3dadf06c6bb042a5a19b02645ecd5d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/422534 Commit-Ready: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="422534" owner_email="ntang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/34/422534/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9490928e71c3b3e1dbfba7df25f0d265ef840bbd" commit="6909592908e356efd7079f9b034c69d37ef8bce4" commit_message="media-libs/mesa: Update to 37d63b50b196afe61b4d7c33b1118a49a5e1e13f  This updates mesa to 37d63b50b196afe61b4d7c33b1118a49a5e1e13f  BUG=b:33532848 TEST=graphics still works  Change-Id: I9490928e71c3b3e1dbfba7df25f0d265ef840bbd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423331 Commit-Ready: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423331" owner_email="hshi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/31/423331/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1f48f098cde3f3f3bb36f16f5372c4d653242195" commit="0a81759df8a41490c61a6c271895d8679d8bc28b" commit_message="net-dns/avahi-daemon: ignore obsolete brillo-debug USE flag  The brillo-debug USE flag was obsolete along the brillo debug link, which depended on the avahi daemon.  BUG=chromium:674648 BUG=chromium:673072 TEST=Remote trybot runs.  Change-Id: I1f48f098cde3f3f3bb36f16f5372c4d653242195 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/377641 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="377641" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/41/377641/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I996d0399ce7e8c86c0ef107b2f97974a44b20334" commit="e650667f3ea9278e64500110dc53242566db1022" commit_message="UPSTREAM: Input: uinput - add new UINPUT_DEV_SETUP and UI_ABS_SETUP ioctl  This adds two new ioctls, UINPUT_DEV_SETUP and UI_ABS_SETUP, that replaces the old device setup method (by write()'ing &quot;struct uinput_user_dev&quot; to the node). The old method is not easily extendable and requires huge payloads. Furthermore, overloading write() without properly versioned objects is error-prone.  Therefore, we introduce two new ioctls to replace the old method.  These ioctls support all features of the old method, plus a &quot;resolution&quot; field for absinfo. Furthermore, it's properly forward-compatible to new ABS codes and a growing &quot;struct input_absinfo&quot; structure.  UI_ABS_SETUP also allows user-space to skip unknown axes if not set.  There is no need to copy the whole array temporarily into the kernel, but instead the caller issues several ioctl where we copy each value manually.  Originally-signed-off-by: David Herrmann &lt;dh.herrmann@gmail.com&gt; Originally-signed-off-by: Benjamin Tissoires &lt;benjamin.tissoires@redhat.com&gt; Originally-reviewed-by: David Herrmann &lt;dh.herrmann@gmail.com&gt; Originally-signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dmitry.torokhov@gmail.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 052876f8e5aec887d22c4d06e54aa5531ffcec75)  BUG=chromium:624181 TEST=Manually built kernel and booted a Reks off it. I then was able to successfully run a piece of software using the new features that were added on that Chromebook.  Change-Id: I996d0399ce7e8c86c0ef107b2f97974a44b20334 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/356736 Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit e54d68d5fe6f6b84b1ca2a4e3270a82e5768abeb) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423255 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423255" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/55/423255/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6097c449a88977b81bf781a489b46856ce8be851" commit="206578bc8f42e689af45e6d8a0a07e5a4b6c52dd" commit_message="cros-workon: Add some incompatible options validation.  There is no way to enforce the sub-directory blacklist if we never copy sources from the user's checkout. This is OK, since this is not the intended use case for the CROS_WORKON_SUBDIR_BLACKLIST option. Let's just validate the ebuilds to be sure.  BUG=chromium:676503 TEST=pre-cq  Change-Id: I6097c449a88977b81bf781a489b46856ce8be851 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423187 Commit-Ready: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="423187" owner_email="pprabhu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/87/423187/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iaea22e1c57abe12bf3133dc17d017657ef9c99de" commit="a09eff04d7c96430c6357bf1de68ade972323c8b" commit_message="Delete obsolete file ROOT_PRESUBMIT.  So the next poor fellow like me doesn't end up trying to fix bugs in it.  BUG=chromium:676699 TEST=None.  Change-Id: Iaea22e1c57abe12bf3133dc17d017657ef9c99de Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423333 Commit-Ready: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423333" owner_email="pprabhu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.google